ode on the wall if you scan this  barcode on your phone it will take you  to marvel.com where you can read a free  she-hulk comic that inspired the series  that is now streaming on disney plus  that we just watched and when she's  waiting outside for her cousin bruce to  come pick her up we see some guys come  out who say ladies night was a bust  meaning they didn't really have any game  and didn't get with any women however  they see jennifer outside and they are  really really pressing her they keep  pressing her and she feels threatened so  of course she turns into she-hulk but  right before she does anything bruce  banner as the hulk jumps on her and  restrains her we cut back to bruce's  place in mexico jen wakes up and looks  for bruce and actually when she's going  to look for bruce she stumbles upon what  looks to be an old iron man helmet that  or either it is an old iron legion  helmet but what's really cool is that  when jennifer actually sees the helmet  you can hear the old avengers theme play  in the background an awesome and epic  easter egg here and it fits perfectly  into this episode as bruce consistently  brings up tony stark reinforcing the  fact that they were best friends science  bros now jen eventually finds bruce  banner down in his lab back in hulk form  or as he calls it smart hulk which is  something that fans actually termed and  it's funny that they actually do kind of  address that and kind of break the  fourth wall here when bruce says you  don't really have a say in what people  call you which is clever because the  fans are the ones who originally started  calling him smart hulk that and  professor hulk now what's really funny  is that smart hulk goes on to explain  that the lab was given to him by tony  stark his friend probably his best  friend and you can tell that he's proud  of that he says tony tony stark and he  gets a little grin on his face but then  he jokes about how tony said it was a  loner and that at any moment in time he  could sweep by and pick it all up again  and you can actually see the sadness on  his face when he says that because of  course now sadly tony is gone and you  can tell by the look on his face that he  misses him here we actually learned that  the hulk uses jennifer's blood to fix  his own arm clearly their blood and  genes are actually a little bit  different they do have the same factors  that allow them to synthesize gamma  radiation but it does seem like gins  does it a little bit better or at least  differently because as we find out when  jyn turns into she-hulk she actually  retains her consciousness and she is  still in control very different than  bruce banner and the hulk they are two  different people but it looks like jyn  and she hulk are actually kind of the  same person the only thing that changes  is her body and of course her strength  and everything that comes with being  she-hulk but her consciousness is  totally intact and she is totally in  charge not wrestling with a she-hulk as  a different person but she herself is  still the same person which blows bruce  spanner's mind away now bruce tells her  that there's no way she's going back to  a normal life after this she is now a  hulk and he tells her that she's  basically going to have to change her  entire life but jennifer walters has  been set on being a lawyer for a very  long time she finally graduated past the  bar exam has her own office working at  the da's office right now and there's no  way that she's not going back to that  and bruce is essentially saying that she  can't because she needs to keep her  anger in check because her turning into  the hulk jeopardizes a lot of people's  safety so she basically needs to stay  there so bruce can run some tests to  figure out really what makes her tick  and turn into she-hulk however after  doing a bunch of these tests they  realize that jyn can control it she can  turn into she-hulk when she wants to and  she can actually turn back when she  wants to so the threat of a true hulk  bursting out and raging and not having  any control whatsoever and doing  destruction and harm to other people  that's not really there the threat of  that isn't there because jyn ultimately  has control and actually at a point in  the comics jennifer walters actually  prefers to remain in she-hulk form for a  long time now when she's with bruce  banner here in mexico and they're trying  to figure out how she turns into  she-hulk and how exactly she is as a  she-hulk there are some really cool  references and easter eggs when they are  trying to determine how she-hulk can  turn back into jennifer walters she  asked smart hulk how when he was the  hulk he would turn back into bruce  banner here bruce says usually i'd fall  out of a jet or get knocked out by a  robot and i'd wake up as banner now the  first part falling out of the jet is a  reference to the very first avengers  film where the hulk hulked out on the  carrier he jumped on a fighter plane and  eventually jumped off and landed on  earth he awakened as bruce banner the  second part is the ultron fight in  avengers age of ultron and of course he  goes on to talk about natasha singing  him a lullaby which we saw in avengers  age of ultron as well and it's really  funny that he can't actually explain how  the lullaby would bring him back into  bruce banner form however i think we all  know it's because of the love so  jennifer tries to conclude that being  unconscious is the key to turning back  into human form however bruce goes on to  explain that one time he was the hulk  for two years and of course we know that  that was the time of thor ragnarok and  during that time he saw a previously  recorded message of natasha talking to  bruce banner and that's what turned the  hulk back into bruce we then have a  montage of bruce banner essentially  training jennifer on how to be a hulk we  see them throwing boulders and getting  really competitive with each other and  